---
title: Chicken Satay
servings: 3
course: dinner
tags: chicken, satay, main course, asian, peanut, grilled, baked, danish
source: https://recipes.cooklang.org/recipes/5626
time: 1h15m
---

= Marinade =
Mix @fresh ginger{3%tsp}, @garlic{2%tsp}, @curry powder{1.5%tsp}, @salt{1.5%tsp}, @oil{3%tbsp} and @coconut milk{3%tbsp} into a marinade.

Add @chicken breast{500%g} cut into strips (1 x 2 x 10 cm) and let it marinate for at least ~{1%hour} at room temperature, preferably up to ~{24%hours} in the #fridge{}.

= Cooking =
Soak the #skewers{} in water so they do not burn. Thread the meat onto the #skewers{}.

Cook on the #grill{} for ~{5-10%minutes} or in the #oven{} at 225°C for ~{10-15%minutes}.

= Sauce =
Heat @&coconut milk{355%ml} to boiling point.

Add @red curry paste{2%tsp}, @peanut butter{2%tbsp}, @sugar{1%tbsp}, @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and @peanut{150%g} chopped, one at a time while stirring in the mentioned order. Do not use the #lid{} and do not let the sauce boil vigorously, as it separates easily.
